\f1\b0  (the status line also shows the ping result).\
\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	4	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The camera pane opens automatically (when the robot's camera service is running).\
\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	5	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Operating controls: 
\f0\b \uc0\u55357 \u56341  STAND / \u55358 \u56977  SIT
\f1\b0 , the action buttons (dance, hello, flips\'85), the two joysticks (left: forward/back + turn, right: slide), 
\f0\b STOP
\f1\b0  and 
\f0\b E-STOP
\f1\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 4. Before you move the robot\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Clear the area (about 5 m) and keep the physical E-stop within reach \'97 it always overrides the software.\
\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The robot must be 
\f0\b standing
\f1\b0 : driving commands are ignored while it is sitting or lying down.\
\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
If the header shows 
\f0\b E-STOP
\f1\b0  latched, press 
\f0\b \uc0\u10226  Return
\f1\b0  to re-arm. While latched, no command is sent.\
\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Both joysticks are spring-centred: release = stop. Holding a position keeps driving until released.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 5. Troubleshooting\
\pard\pardeftab720\li720\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The page does not open:
\f1\b0  your device is not on the same network as the console computer, or the IP is wrong. Re-join the robot Wi-Fi / LAN and re-check the IP.\

\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Page opens but not connected:
\f1\b0  verify Advanced \uc0\u8594  Robot IP matches the network (2.1 on robot Wi-Fi, 1.120 on LAN), and that the robot is powered and awake.\

\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Buttons are greyed until connected:
\f1\b0  expected. They enable automatically on connect.\

\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Commands seem to do nothing:
\f1\b0  robot not standing, or software E-stop latched (press \uc0\u10226  Return). Note that UDP gives no acknowledgement \'97 confirm motion visually.\

\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
No camera:
\f1\b0  the robot's camera service must be running on the robot. The console retries automatically every ~8 s.\

\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 	\'95	\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
No battery / IMU readout:
\f1\b0  requires a one-time setting on the robot (telemetry target in ~/jy_exe/conf/network.toml). Driving works without it.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\pardirnatural\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf0 Security note:
\f1\i0  the console is a local service without authentication \'97 keep it on trusted, local networks and close the browser session when finished.\
